# Antigravity AI Project Rules: RouteTrust

## Project Mission
RouteTrust is a probabilistic transit reliability and leave-by advisor built using LightGBM quantile regression (tau = 0.10, 0.50, 0.90), FastAPI, Streamlit, and SQLite in WAL mode.

## Ground Truth Documentation
Always refer to and adhere strictly to the specification files located in `/docs`:
- docs/01-Product-Requirements.md
- docs/02-Technical-Architecture.md
- docs/03-Security-Access.md
- docs/04-Frontend-Spec.md
- docs/feature_list.md

## Architecture & Code Standards
- Python Version: 3.11.
- Backend: FastAPI with Pydantic v2 schemas and SQLAlchemy 2.0 ORM.
- Frontend: Streamlit running on port 7860 communicating via HTTP loopback to FastAPI on port 8000.
- Database: SQLite (routetrust.db) strictly configured with PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL; and busy_timeout=15000.
- Machine Learning: LightGBM Quantile Regressors (objective="quantile") with monotonic rearrangement sorting to guarantee Q10 <= Q50 <= Q90.
- Safety Clamps: Never allow leave-by time recommendations to be later than scheduled departure (leave_by <= t_arrive - S), enforcing the Early Departure Guard.
- Weather Service: Async Open-Meteo client with a strict 2.0-second timeout; always fall back to SQLite weather_fallbacks on failure and tag weather_source = "historical_fallback". Never default to clear weather silently.

